-#### Opacity Split for Cloning
-- [S3] A method to initialize the opacity of cloned Gaussians to maintain transmittance consistency, preventing the cloned child from having less impact than the parent alone.
-- [S3] $o_{\text{new}} = 1 - \sqrt{1 - o_{\text{old}}}$ where $o_{\text{new}}$ is the opacity of both the parent and the clone child after cloning, and $o_{\text{old}}$ is the parent's opacity before cloning.
-- [S3] In standard 3DGS, the cloned child inherits the parent's opacity, which decreases the impact of any subsequent Gaussian in the alpha blending process because the parent and child together have greater transmittance impact than the parent alone.
